If a patient has a shorter-duration-opioid-use then every clinician may use a ten-percent-of-original-dose-per-week-or-slower-first-taper-stage for the patient.
If a patient has a shorter-duration-opioid-use then every clinician may use a ten-percent-of-remaining-dose-per-week-after-approximately-thirty-percent-of-original-dose-second-taper-stage for the patient.
